{"id":"p21-l04","minutes":40,"summary":"Where can a four-line robot hold a load, and how heavy a load? You turn the tension distribution into a capacity number at every point, map it over a room, and find out why the centre is the best place near the floor and the worst place near the ceiling.","html":"<h2 id=\"two-questions-about-a-workspace\">Two questions about a workspace</h2>\n<p>“Can the robot get there?” has a cable-robot answer that is different from an arm’s. Every point inside the four anchors is geometrically reachable: you only have to wind the lines to the right lengths. The real question is whether the lines can <strong>hold</strong> the robot there, with every tension between zero and some limit. The set of poses where they can is called the <em>wrench-feasible workspace</em>, and it shrinks as the payload grows.</p>\n<p>The second question turns it round: at a given point, what is the heaviest load the lines can hold? Lesson 3 already has the ingredients.</p>\n<h2 id=\"capacity-at-a-point\">Capacity at a point</h2>\n<p>With a tension floor of zero, every tension in the static solution is proportional to the hanging mass: <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6349em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathbf\">t</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">m</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord boldsymbol\" style=\"margin-right:0.1347em;\">τ</span></span></span></span></span></span>, where <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord boldsymbol\" style=\"margin-right:0.1347em;\">τ</span></span></span></span></span></span> is the tension per kilogram. The spare degree of freedom lets us choose <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord boldsymbol\" style=\"margin-right:0.1347em;\">τ</span></span></span></span></span></span> along a line, so we pick the one with the smallest peak, subject to <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.786em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1132em;\">τ</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3117em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.1132em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">i</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≥</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0</span></span></span></span>:</p>\n<div class=\"math-scroll\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">m</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord text mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">max</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathbf\">p</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:2.2963em;vertical-align:-0.936em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mopen nulldelimiter\"></span><span class=\"mfrac\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.3603em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.314em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mop\"><span class=\"mop\">min</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3361em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">λ</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\"> </span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\"><span class=\"mop\">max</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3117em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">i</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\"> </span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1132em;\">τ</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3117em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.1132em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">i</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">λ</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.23em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"frac-line\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.677em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">T</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.1389em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord text mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">max</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.936em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose nulldelimiter\"></span></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:2em;\"></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord boldsymbol\" style=\"margin-right:0.1347em;\">τ</span></span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">λ</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8694em;vertical-align:-0.2861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord boldsymbol\" style=\"margin-right:0.1347em;\">τ</span></span></span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">p</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">λ</span><span class=\"mord mathbf\">n</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\"> </span><span class=\"mspace\"> </span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1132em;\">τ</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3117em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.1132em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">i</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">λ</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≥</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.</span></span></span></span></span></div>\n<p>The inner function is the maximum of four straight lines in <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">λ</span></span></span></span>, so it is convex and piecewise linear. Its minimum sits either at an end of the feasible interval or where two of the lines cross. Checking at most eight candidates gives the exact answer, fast enough to run 1,600 times every time the simulator redraws its map.</p>\n<p>Three consequences fall straight out of the formula:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Capacity is linear in the limit.</strong> Halve the allowed tension and you halve the payload everywhere. A map for one limit is a map for all of them, rescaled.</li>\n<li><strong>The steepness of the lines is everything.</strong> At the centre all four share equally, so <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.5806em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">m</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord text mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">max</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">4</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">T</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.1389em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord text mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">max</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\">sin</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">θ</span><span class=\"mord\">/</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">g</span></span></span></span>. Low pivot, steep lines, big payload.</li>\n<li><strong>The mass is everything that hangs.</strong> The gripper, its pole and the power line it hangs from all count against the same tension. The payload you can pick up is what is left.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"the-shape-of-the-map\">The shape of the map</h2>\n<p>Take Stringman’s 7 × 7 × 3 m example room with every line limited to 28 N, the point at which Stringman’s motors relax.</p>\n<div class=\"table-scroll\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Pivot height</th>\n<th>Lowest in the room</th>\n<th>Mean</th>\n<th>Highest</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>0.6 m</td>\n<td>2.97 kg</td>\n<td>3.71 kg</td>\n<td>4.86 kg</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>1.2 m</td>\n<td>2.66 kg</td>\n<td>3.11 kg</td>\n<td>3.82 kg</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>1.8 m</td>\n<td>1.89 kg</td>\n<td>2.32 kg</td>\n<td>2.94 kg</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2.4 m</td>\n<td>0.99 kg</td>\n<td>1.29 kg</td>\n<td>2.82 kg</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n<p>Near the floor the best spot is the centre, 5.15 kg with the gripper on the floor, because the four lines share the load at the steepest common angle. Near the ceiling it flips. At 2.4 m the centre lines are almost horizontal and the best places are under the anchors, where one line hangs nearly straight down and carries the load alone. Close under the ceiling and halfway along a wall is the worst: 0.165 kg at <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">3.4</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2.9</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span>, because two lines run along the wall and two run almost flat across the room.</p>\n<p>Neufangled publishes its own version of this map on its home page, with an interactive version for your own room dimensions. Their figure is computed at the rated torque of the DM-H6215 motors, not at the 28 N relax limit, and it quotes up to 2 kg near the floor and 1.25 kg on average over the work volume. In this lesson’s point-mass model, 2 kg at the floor centre corresponds to a working tension of about 10.9 N per line, and a 1.25 kg mean to roughly 15 N if you count pivot heights from 0.5 to 2.9 m. We cannot reproduce their figure exactly because we do not have their spool radius or their definition of the work volume, but the order of magnitude says something useful: the relax limit sits about twice above the tension the robot normally works at, so ordinary motion does not trip it.</p>\n\n<figure class=\"fig\"><div class=\"fig-body\"><div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"cablebot\" data-args=\"{&quot;preset&quot;:&quot;workspace&quot;}\"></div></div><figcaption>Capacity map. The slice is drawn at the pivot height; coral cells cannot hold the payload within the tension limit. Change the payload, the limit, or the room, and drag the gripper up to see the centre go from best to worst.</figcaption></figure>\n<h2 id=\"worked-example-does-1-5-kg-fit-everywhere-at-desk-height\">Worked example: does 1.5 kg fit everywhere at desk height?</h2>\n<p>A 1.5 kg load in the example room, gripper at a 0.75 m desk, so the pivot is at 1.25 m, and the full 28 N available.</p>\n<ol>\n<li>At the centre, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\">sin</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">θ</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1.1634em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1.75/</span><span class=\"mord sqrt\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.9134em;\"><span class=\"svg-align\" style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\" style=\"padding-left:0.833em;\"><span class=\"mord\">24.5</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1.7</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">5</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.7401em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.989em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-2.8734em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"hide-tail\" style=\"min-width:0.853em;height:1.08em;\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"400em\" height=\"1.08em\" viewBox=\"0 0 400000 1080\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMinYMin slice\"><path d=\"M95,702\nc-2.7,0,-7.17,-2.7,-13.5,-8c-5.8,-5.3,-9.5,-10,-9.5,-14\nc0,-2,0.3,-3.3,1,-4c1.3,-2.7,23.83,-20.7,67.5,-54\nc44.2,-33.3,65.8,-50.3,66.5,-51c1.3,-1.3,3,-2,5,-2c4.7,0,8.7,3.3,12,10\ns173,378,173,378c0.7,0,35.3,-71,104,-213c68.7,-142,137.5,-285,206.5,-429\nc69,-144,104.5,-217.7,106.5,-221\nl0 -0\nc5.3,-9.3,12,-14,20,-14\nH400000v40H845.2724\ns-225.272,467,-225.272,467s-235,486,-235,486c-2.7,4.7,-9,7,-19,7\nc-6,0,-10,-1,-12,-3s-194,-422,-194,-422s-65,47,-65,47z\nM834 80h400000v40h-400000z\"/></svg></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1266em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.333</span></span></span></span>, so <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.5806em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">m</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord text mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">max</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">4</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">28</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.333/9.81</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">3.80</span></span></span></span> kg.</li>\n<li>The lowest capacity at that height, close to a wall, is about 2.55 kg.</li>\n<li>Even that leaves room for the gripper’s own weight. With the working tension nearer 11 N, though, the same map scales by 11/28, and the wall becomes about 1.0 kg. A 1.5 kg load at desk height near the walls would then need the motors to work above their rated tension.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>That last line is the kind of check worth doing before you promise a payload: decide which limit you mean, rated or trip, and read the map at that limit.</p>\n<h2 id=\"code-it-from-scratch\">Code it from scratch</h2>\n\n<div class=\"code-card\" data-code=\"0\"><div class=\"code-head\"><span class=\"fname\" translate=\"no\">capacity_map.py</span><button class=\"btn btn-quiet btn-small\" type=\"button\" data-copy=\"0\">Copy</button><button class=\"btn btn-quiet btn-small\" type=\"button\" data-download=\"0\">Download</button></div><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code class=\"language-python\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">import</span> numpy <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">as</span> np, time\n\nG = <span class=\"hljs-number\">9.81</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">anchors</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">w, d, h</span>):\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> np.array([[-w/<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>, -d/<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>, h], [w/<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>, -d/<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>, h], [w/<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>, d/<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>, h], [-w/<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>, d/<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>, h]])\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">capacity</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">A, p, t_max</span>):\n    <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;&quot;&quot;largest hanging mass at pivot p with every tension in [0, t_max]&quot;&quot;&quot;</span>\n    v = A - p\n    U = (v / np.linalg.norm(v, axis=<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>)[:, <span class=\"hljs-literal\">None</span>]).T\n    tau = U.T @ np.linalg.solve(U @ U.T, [<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>, G])            <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># tensions per kg, minimum norm</span>\n    n = np.linalg.svd(U)[<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>][-<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>]\n    lo = <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">max</span>([-tau[i] / n[i] <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> i <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">range</span>(<span class=\"hljs-number\">4</span>) <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> n[i] &gt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">1e-12</span>], default=-np.inf)\n    hi = <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">min</span>([-tau[i] / n[i] <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> i <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">range</span>(<span class=\"hljs-number\">4</span>) <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> n[i] &lt; -<span class=\"hljs-number\">1e-12</span>], default=np.inf)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> lo &gt; hi:\n        <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.0</span>                                             <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># no all-pulling solution: outside the workspace</span>\n    cands = [lo, hi] + [(tau[j] - tau[i]) / (n[i] - n[j]) <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> i <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">range</span>(<span class=\"hljs-number\">4</span>) <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> j <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">range</span>(i+<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">4</span>) <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(n[i] - n[j]) &gt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">1e-12</span>]\n    peak = <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">min</span>(np.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">max</span>(tau + c * n) <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> c <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> cands <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> lo - <span class=\"hljs-number\">1e-9</span> &lt;= c &lt;= hi + <span class=\"hljs-number\">1e-9</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> t_max / peak\n\nA = anchors(<span class=\"hljs-number\">7</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">7</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">3</span>)\nc0 = capacity(A, np.array([<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.5</span>]), <span class=\"hljs-number\">28</span>)\ns = <span class=\"hljs-number\">2.5</span> / np.sqrt(<span class=\"hljs-number\">24.5</span> + <span class=\"hljs-number\">2.5</span>**<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>)\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(c0 - <span class=\"hljs-number\">4</span> * <span class=\"hljs-number\">28</span> * s / G) &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">1e-9</span>                       <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># centre: four equal lines, m = 4 T sin(theta) / g</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">print</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">f&quot;centre, gripper on the floor: <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{c0:<span class=\"hljs-number\">.2</span>f}</span> kg at 28 N&quot;</span>)\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> p, want <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> [((<span class=\"hljs-number\">1.0</span>, -<span class=\"hljs-number\">0.5</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.9</span>), <span class=\"hljs-number\">3.91</span>), ((<span class=\"hljs-number\">3.0</span>, -<span class=\"hljs-number\">0.5</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.9</span>), <span class=\"hljs-number\">3.17</span>), ((<span class=\"hljs-number\">3.4</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">2.9</span>), <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.165</span>), ((<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">2.5</span>), <span class=\"hljs-number\">1.15</span>)]:\n    c = capacity(A, np.array(p), <span class=\"hljs-number\">28</span>); <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">print</span>(p, <span class=\"hljs-string\">f&quot;<span class=\"hljs-subst\">{c:<span class=\"hljs-number\">.3</span>f}</span> kg&quot;</span>); <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(c - want) &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.006</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> capacity(A, np.array([<span class=\"hljs-number\">4.0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">1.0</span>]), <span class=\"hljs-number\">28</span>) == <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>          <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># beyond the footprint</span>\nt0 = time.time()\nxs = (np.arange(<span class=\"hljs-number\">24</span>) + <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.5</span>) / <span class=\"hljs-number\">24</span> * <span class=\"hljs-number\">7</span> - <span class=\"hljs-number\">3.5</span>\nzs = <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.5</span> + (np.arange(<span class=\"hljs-number\">12</span>) + <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.5</span>) / <span class=\"hljs-number\">12</span> * <span class=\"hljs-number\">2.4</span>\ncaps = np.array([[[capacity(A, np.array([x, y, z]), <span class=\"hljs-number\">28</span>) <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> x <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> xs] <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> y <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> xs] <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> z <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> zs])\n<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">print</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">f&quot;mean over pivot heights 0.5-2.9 m: <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{caps.mean():<span class=\"hljs-number\">.2</span>f}</span> kg (<span class=\"hljs-subst\">{time.time()-t0:<span class=\"hljs-number\">.1</span>f}</span> s)&quot;</span>)\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> z, layer <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">zip</span>(zs[::<span class=\"hljs-number\">3</span>], caps[::<span class=\"hljs-number\">3</span>]):\n    <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">print</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">f&quot;  z = <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{z:<span class=\"hljs-number\">.1</span>f}</span> m: min <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{layer.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">min</span>():<span class=\"hljs-number\">.2</span>f}</span>, mean <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{layer.mean():<span class=\"hljs-number\">.2</span>f}</span>, max <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{layer.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">max</span>():<span class=\"hljs-number\">.2</span>f}</span> kg&quot;</span>)\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> <span class=\"hljs-number\">2.2</span> &lt; caps.mean() &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">2.45</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-comment\"># near the floor the centre is best; near the ceiling it is the worst place in the room</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> capacity(A, np.array([<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.6</span>]), <span class=\"hljs-number\">28</span>) &gt; capacity(A, np.array([<span class=\"hljs-number\">3.2</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">3.2</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.6</span>]), <span class=\"hljs-number\">28</span>)\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> capacity(A, np.array([<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">2.8</span>]), <span class=\"hljs-number\">28</span>) &lt; capacity(A, np.array([<span class=\"hljs-number\">3.2</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">3.2</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">2.8</span>]), <span class=\"hljs-number\">28</span>)\n<span class=\"hljs-comment\"># capacity is linear in the limit: halve the allowed tension, halve the payload</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(capacity(A, np.array([<span class=\"hljs-number\">1.0</span>, -<span class=\"hljs-number\">0.5</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.9</span>]), <span class=\"hljs-number\">14</span>) * <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span> - capacity(A, np.array([<span class=\"hljs-number\">1.0</span>, -<span class=\"hljs-number\">0.5</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.9</span>]), <span class=\"hljs-number\">28</span>)) &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">1e-9</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-comment\"># what working tension would give 2 kg at the floor centre, and 1.25 kg on average?</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">print</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">f&quot;tension for 2 kg at the floor centre: <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{<span class=\"hljs-number\">28</span> * <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span> / c0:<span class=\"hljs-number\">.1</span>f}</span> N; for a 1.25 kg mean: <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{<span class=\"hljs-number\">28</span> * <span class=\"hljs-number\">1.25</span> / caps.mean():<span class=\"hljs-number\">.1</span>f}</span> N&quot;</span>)\n<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">print</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;PASS&quot;</span>)</code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"in-practice\">In practice</h2>\n<p>Hang the anchors as high as you can and as close to the true corners as the room allows. Every centimetre of height steepens the lines and raises the whole map; Neufangled’s sizing guidance gives the range of room shapes it supports, from 2 to 10 m across the diagonal and a length-to-height ratio between 0.9 and 2.5, which is the same geometry argument in product form. Keep heavy work near the floor and the centre, and treat the space close under the ceiling as a place to travel through, not a place to lift.</p>\n<h2 id=\"exercises\">Exercises</h2>\n\n<div class=\"exercise\"><div class=\"ex-q\"><p>Show that at the centre of a square room the capacity is <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">4</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">T</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.1389em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord text mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">max</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\">sin</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">θ</span><span class=\"mord\">/</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">g</span></span></span></span> and compute it with the pivot at 1.5 m.</p>\n</div><details><summary>Show the solution</summary><div class=\"ex-s\"><p>By symmetry the minimum-norm tensions are equal and the minimax over the null space cannot do better than equal (moving along <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span> raises one pair). Four equal tensions <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">T</span></span></span></span> give a vertical force <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">4</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">T</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\">sin</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">θ</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.625em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">m</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">g</span></span></span></span>. With <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\">sin</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">θ</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1.5/5.172</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.290</span></span></span></span>: <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">4</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">28</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.290/9.81</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">3.31</span></span></span></span> kg.</p>\n</div></details></div>\n\n<div class=\"exercise\"><div class=\"ex-q\"><p>Why does the best spot move from the centre to the corners as the pivot rises?</p>\n</div><details><summary>Show the solution</summary><div class=\"ex-s\"><p>At the centre the lines become shallower as the pivot rises, and <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\">sin</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">θ</span></span></span></span> falls towards zero at the ceiling. Under an anchor one line becomes nearly vertical and can carry the whole weight on its own at a tension close to <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.625em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">m</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">g</span></span></span></span>, so the corner capacity stays near <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">T</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.1389em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord text mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">max</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord\">/</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">g</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2.85</span></span></span></span> kg all the way up.</p>\n</div></details></div>\n<h2 id=\"quiz\">Quiz</h2>\n\n<div class=\"quiz\" data-quiz=\"p21-l04\"></div>\n\n<h2 id=\"sources\">Sources</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Neufangled, <a href=\"https://neufangled.com/\">Stringman home page and tech specs</a> (payload map at rated torque in a 7 × 7 × 3 m room, up to 2 kg near the floor and 1.25 kg average, DM-H6215 1 N·m actuators, room sizes 2 to 10 m diagonal and length-to-height 0.9 to 2.5, 28 N relax limit).</li>\n<li>P. Bosscher, A. Riechel and I. Ebert-Uphoff, <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1109/tro.2006.878967\">“Wrench-feasible workspace generation for cable-driven robots”</a>, <em>IEEE Transactions on Robotics</em>, 2006.</li>\n<li>A. Pott, <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-319-76138-1\"><em>Cable-Driven Parallel Robots: Theory and Application</em></a>, Springer, 2018.</li>\n</ul>\n","toc":[{"id":"two-questions-about-a-workspace","title":"Two questions about a workspace"},{"id":"capacity-at-a-point","title":"Capacity at a point"},{"id":"the-shape-of-the-map","title":"The shape of the map"},{"id":"worked-example-does-1-5-kg-fit-everywhere-at-desk-height","title":"Worked example: does 1.5 kg fit everywhere at desk height?"},{"id":"code-it-from-scratch","title":"Code it from scratch"},{"id":"in-practice","title":"In practice"},{"id":"exercises","title":"Exercises"},{"id":"quiz","title":"Quiz"},{"id":"sources","title":"Sources"}],"quiz":[{"id":"p21-l04-q1","type":"num","q":"<p>Capacity at the centre of the 7 × 7 × 3 m room, gripper on the floor (pivot 0.5 m), with a 28 N limit (kg)?</p>\n","explain":"<p>4 T sin θ / g with sin θ = 2.5/5.545.</p>\n","answer":5.15,"tol":0.005,"unit":""},{"id":"p21-l04-q2","type":"mc","q":"<p>You lower the tension limit from 28 N to 14 N. What happens to the capacity map?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Tensions scale with the mass, so capacity is linear in the limit.</p>\n","options":["The centre goes up","Only the corners change","Every value halves","Nothing, capacity depends only on geometry"],"answer":2},{"id":"p21-l04-q3","type":"mc","q":"<p>Close under the ceiling, where does a four-line robot hold the most?</p>\n","explain":"<p>At the centre the lines are nearly flat there; under an anchor one line can take the whole load.</p>\n","options":["At the centre","Halfway along a wall","Everywhere equally","Under an anchor, where one line hangs nearly vertical"],"answer":3},{"id":"p21-l04-q4","type":"num","q":"<p>Capacity at the centre with the pivot at 1.5 m and a 28 N limit (kg)?</p>\n","explain":"<p>sin θ = 0.290.</p>\n","answer":3.31,"tol":0.005,"unit":""},{"id":"p21-l04-q5","type":"mc","q":"<p>The capacity of the lines is 3 kg at a point and the gripper weighs 0.6 kg. What can it pick up there?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Everything that hangs counts against the same tensions.</p>\n","options":["3.6 kg","0.6 kg","2.4 kg","3 kg"],"answer":2},{"id":"p21-l04-q6","type":"num","q":"<p>In the point-mass model, what working tension per line gives 2 kg at the floor centre (N)?</p>\n","explain":"<p>T = m g / (4 sin θ).</p>\n","answer":10.9,"tol":0.01,"unit":""}],"code":[{"file":"capacity_map.py","lang":"python","src":"import numpy as np, time\n\nG = 9.81\ndef anchors(w, d, h):\n    return np.array([[-w/2, -d/2, h], [w/2, -d/2, h], [w/2, d/2, h], [-w/2, d/2, h]])\n\ndef capacity(A, p, t_max):\n    \"\"\"largest hanging mass at pivot p with every tension in [0, t_max]\"\"\"\n    v = A - p\n    U = (v / np.linalg.norm(v, axis=1)[:, None]).T\n    tau = U.T @ np.linalg.solve(U @ U.T, [0, 0, G])            # tensions per kg, minimum norm\n    n = np.linalg.svd(U)[2][-1]\n    lo = max([-tau[i] / n[i] for i in range(4) if n[i] > 1e-12], default=-np.inf)\n    hi = min([-tau[i] / n[i] for i in range(4) if n[i] < -1e-12], default=np.inf)\n    if lo > hi:\n        return 0.0                                             # no all-pulling solution: outside the workspace\n    cands = [lo, hi] + [(tau[j] - tau[i]) / (n[i] - n[j]) for i in range(4) for j in range(i+1, 4) if abs(n[i] - n[j]) > 1e-12]\n    peak = min(np.max(tau + c * n) for c in cands if lo - 1e-9 <= c <= hi + 1e-9)\n    return t_max / peak\n\nA = anchors(7, 7, 3)\nc0 = capacity(A, np.array([0, 0, 0.5]), 28)\ns = 2.5 / np.sqrt(24.5 + 2.5**2)\nassert abs(c0 - 4 * 28 * s / G) < 1e-9                       # centre: four equal lines, m = 4 T sin(theta) / g\nprint(f\"centre, gripper on the floor: {c0:.2f} kg at 28 N\")\nfor p, want in [((1.0, -0.5, 0.9), 3.91), ((3.0, -0.5, 0.9), 3.17), ((3.4, 0, 2.9), 0.165), ((0, 0, 2.5), 1.15)]:\n    c = capacity(A, np.array(p), 28); print(p, f\"{c:.3f} kg\"); assert abs(c - want) < 0.006\nassert capacity(A, np.array([4.0, 0, 1.0]), 28) == 0          # beyond the footprint\nt0 = time.time()\nxs = (np.arange(24) + 0.5) / 24 * 7 - 3.5\nzs = 0.5 + (np.arange(12) + 0.5) / 12 * 2.4\ncaps = np.array([[[capacity(A, np.array([x, y, z]), 28) for x in xs] for y in xs] for z in zs])\nprint(f\"mean over pivot heights 0.5-2.9 m: {caps.mean():.2f} kg ({time.time()-t0:.1f} s)\")\nfor z, layer in zip(zs[::3], caps[::3]):\n    print(f\"  z = {z:.1f} m: min {layer.min():.2f}, mean {layer.mean():.2f}, max {layer.max():.2f} kg\")\n\nassert 2.2 < caps.mean() < 2.45\n# near the floor the centre is best; near the ceiling it is the worst place in the room\nassert capacity(A, np.array([0, 0, 0.6]), 28) > capacity(A, np.array([3.2, 3.2, 0.6]), 28)\nassert capacity(A, np.array([0, 0, 2.8]), 28) < capacity(A, np.array([3.2, 3.2, 2.8]), 28)\n# capacity is linear in the limit: halve the allowed tension, halve the payload\nassert abs(capacity(A, np.array([1.0, -0.5, 0.9]), 14) * 2 - capacity(A, np.array([1.0, -0.5, 0.9]), 28)) < 1e-9\n# what working tension would give 2 kg at the floor centre, and 1.25 kg on average?\nprint(f\"tension for 2 kg at the floor centre: {28 * 2 / c0:.1f} N; for a 1.25 kg mean: {28 * 1.25 / caps.mean():.1f} N\")\nprint(\"PASS\")"}]}